# Port map for scripts/tailscale-serve.sh. Copy to tailscale-serve-port-map,
# which is gitignored — the real mapping names which services this machine
# runs, so it stays out of the repo.
#
# One app per line: <https port> <local port> <name>
#   https port  the tailnet-only port the certificate is served on; must be
#               unique, and must not collide with a port the host already binds
#   local port  reached over loopback, so an app bound to 127.0.0.1 works too
#   name        label for the output only
#
# Take https ports from the reserved 44xx block. Blank lines and # comments are
# ignored. `serve` is per-node, so each machine needs its own copy listing only
# the apps it runs.

1234 5678  first-app
2345 6789  second-app
3456 7890  third-app
